  "answer_text": "# Welch Allyn Ophthalmology Tools\n\nWelch Allyn is a globally recognized manufacturer of medical diagnostic equipment, offering a comprehensive portfolio of ophthalmic instruments such as ophthalmoscopes, retinoscopes, and vision screeners. Here is an overview of their key ophthalmology tools:\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udc41\ufe0f 1. **PanOptic Plus Ophthalmoscope**\nThe Welch Allyn Ophthalmic Sets feature the wide-view PanOptic Plus Ophthalmoscope, and all portable ophthalmic sets now include ophthalmoscopes with long-lasting LED illumination.\n\nDesigned with long-lasting LED lamps and DuraShock\u2122 for durability, the PanOptic Plus also features Quick Eye\u2122 alignment technology that helps direct the patient's gaze for faster, easier exams. Two lights on the patient side help guide their gaze for better optic disc alignment.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udd26 2. **Direct Ophthalmoscope (Standard)**\nWelch Allyn also offers a standard **Direct Ophthalmoscope** as part of their handheld instrument line. This is a traditional tool used for routine eye fundus examinations.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udd0d 3. **Streak Retinoscope**\nThe **Welch Allyn 18245 Streak Retinoscope** is one of their popular handheld ophthalmic instruments. It is used to measure refractive errors and evaluate the optical system of the eye.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udcf1 4. **iExaminer System (SmartBracket)**\nThe **iExaminer SmartBracket** allows clinicians to capture and share eye images when paired with a smart device and the iExaminer Pro App. This system bridges traditional ophthalmic exams with digital documentation.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udd6f\ufe0f 5. **Transilluminator**\nThe **Welch Allyn 41100 Transilluminator** is another handheld ophthalmic tool in their lineup. It is used to examine the eye and surrounding structures by shining a focused light beam.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udc41\ufe0f 6. **Spot Vision Screener**\nThe **Spot Vision Screener** is a handheld, portable device designed to help quickly and easily detect vision issues on patients as young as six months. It is especially useful in pediatric screenings and primary care settings.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udcf8 7. **RetinaVue 700 Imager**\nThe **RetinaVue 700 Imager** is the latest addition to the RetinaVue care delivery model family, making retinal imaging and retinal exams simple and affordable in primary care.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\uddc2\ufe0f 8. **Accessories & Supporting Tools**\nWelch Allyn also provides a wide range of supporting ophthalmic accessories including **fixation cards, near test cards, occluders, prisms, eye charts, color tests, potential acuity meters, and rechargeable power handles**.\n\n---\n\n## \u26a1 Power Handles\nAll ophthalmic sets include Welch Allyn 3.5V rechargeable power handles, ensuring consistent and reliable illumination during examinations.\n\n---\n\nThese tools are widely used by **ophthalmologists, optometrists, primary care physicians, and pediatricians** for comprehensive eye exams and vision screening. They are now distributed under the **Hillrom** brand following the acquisition of Welch Allyn.",
